{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.LiftingDescent.tm_transient_localisation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.tm_transient_localisation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.TransientLocalisationNormEquality.norm_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.TransientLocalisationNormEquality.norm_eq","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/tm_transient_localisation.lean#L108-L108","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.TransientLocalisationNormEquality.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.TransientLocalisationNormEquality.mk","kind":"ctor","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/tm_transient_localisation.lean#L107-L107","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.TransientLocalisationNormEquality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.TransientLocalisationNormEquality","kind":"class","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/tm_transient_localisation.lean#L101-L108","doc":"**Conjecture (the block's equality).**  For the multiplicative integral\nof the transient integrand, the norm over `Σ` equals the sum of the\nexceptional-divisor norms.  Content-bearing, deliberately **without an\ninstance**: by `norm_additivity_not_forced` it does not follow from the\ndisc split and support hypotheses alone, and no further input that would\nforce it is established in the corpus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.norm_additivity_not_forced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.norm_additivity_not_forced","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/tm_transient_localisation.lean#L85-L99","doc":"**The equality is not forced by the split.**  There is data in the\nseminormed group `Multiplicative ℝ` satisfying both geometric hypotheses\n(`hsplit` with `N = 2`, and `hsupp` trivially with `div = disc`) for which\n`‖MI∫_Σ‖ ≠ Σᵢ ‖MI∫_{Eᵢ}‖`.  Scope (a): this shows the hypotheses *alone*\ndo not yield the block's equality; it says nothing about the specific\nmultiplicative integral of the transient integrand. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.tm_transient_localisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.tm_transient_localisation","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/tm_transient_localisation.lean#L70-L83","doc":"**Transient-term localisation, derived half (inequality).**\n\nGiven that the transient multiplicative integral over `Σ` is the ordered\nproduct of the disc integrals (`hsplit`) and that each disc integral is the\nexceptional-divisor integral (`hsupp`), its norm is at most the sum of the\nexceptional-divisor norms. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:topological-mass-transient-localisation","label":"lem:topological-mass-transient-localisation","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass-transient-localisation.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.norm_prod_range_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.norm_prod_range_le","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/tm_transient_localisation.lean#L60-L68","doc":"Triangle inequality for an ordered product over `List.range N`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}